    "created_at": "2025-06-28T06:06:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-28T06:19:35Z",
    "body": "Per https://github.com/whatwg/console/issues/245 - there are some newer Browser functionalities that might benefit and be benefited by this kind of functionality now (that likely didn’t exist at the time the Issue was first created/opened).\n\nSpecifically, there are now Read-Only Browser Warnings (in most browsers I’ve tested - specifics in the other Issue). These are often intended to be actionable and some kind of Console Field, Listener, etc. would allow these kinds of issues to be addressed programmatically - say with an eye to the future, would this further benefit AI (allowing common warnings to be auto-configured or resolved programmatically), plugins, various browser extensions, etc.?\n\nAnd at risk of belaboring the obvious (to be a tad bit clearer): most of those kinds of messages _cannot_ be accessed programmatically by developers - the message are emitted, displayed, or printed and cannot trigger an event, say. \n\n\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
